WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
1. Choose Cloud and ISSM
Use Cloud for an AWS run, then select ISSM.
This ISSM cloud workflow runs MATLAB, so this workflow needs a usable license provided by your institution.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Already configured? Prepare reattachment
The masked input is hidden when a managed license is already configured.
Advanced license configuration → save the current ARN privately → clear Existing secret ARN → Use existing secret.
Only the local reference is cleared. The AWS secret stays intact.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:44.000
2. Enter the license address
Paste the network license address supplied by your institution into the masked MATLAB license field.
Use your own institution’s port@server value. The value stays masked on screen.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:56.000
3. Configure the license
Select Configure license.
The existing managed secret is found. Its reference and execution access are reattached.
The typed value is not saved over that secret; the input clears after configuration.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:08.000
4. Confirm the saved reference
MATLAB license configured confirms that the account has a saved license reference.
It does not prove a successful MATLAB checkout. The execution test comes later.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:20.000
5. Connect the institutional bridge
If the license service is private, run the CryoStack Connector where that service is reachable.
Off campus, establish the required institutional VPN connection first. Select Open Connector.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:32.000
6. Pair your Connector
Use your own one-time code to pair the external Connector. The code is hidden here.
This footage shows the pairing prompt and the later Re-check; external code entry is not recorded.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:44.000
7. Re-check the connection
Select Re-check after pairing.
This checks the same-user institutional connection. It does not launch a model or perform a MATLAB checkout.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:56.000
7. Confirm Connector connected
The green CryoStack Connector connected badge confirms the bridge is online.
Keep the Connector and required network connection available until the run ends.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:08.000
8. Review ISSM runtime readiness
Open Review & Launch and confirm ISSM runtime is Ready.
Check the account, model, resources, time limit and estimated charges before launching.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Native MATLAB / ISSM run completed
The actual AWS Batch run succeeded with native exit code 0.
Downloaded runtime provenance reports MATLAB R2024b Update 7 and ISSM 2026.1. This confirms that the configured license path supported actual execution.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Actual licensed execution: saved result
The same accepted native run produced this full saved Vel figure.
Its downloaded provenance reports MATLAB R2024b Update 7 and ISSM 2026.1. The configured license and institutional connection supported actual execution.
